Subject: [channels,rdpewa] optional out-of-process WebAuthn helper backend

When FREERDP_RDPEWA_HELPER names an executable, CTAP MakeCredential and
GetAssertion requests from the server are handed to it as newline-delimited
JSON (base64 CTAP2 request map + rpId/flags/timeout/filterHybrid) and its
CTAP2 response map is returned to the server unchanged. This lets a helper
built on libwebauthn answer with authenticators libfido2 cannot reach, e.g.
phones over the hybrid (caBLE/QR) transport. Falls back to libfido2 when the
helper is not configured or cannot be started. Also decodes the MS-RDPEWA 3.0
"filterHybridTransport" request key, logs request values (incl. webAuthNPara)
at DEBUG, lets FREERDP_RDPEWA_API_VERSION raise the advertised WebAuthn API
version, and FREERDP_RDPEWA_IUVPAA force the platform-authenticator answer.

